{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1333","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Eugene and an array"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Eugene likes working with arrays. And today he needs your help in solving one challenging task."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An array $$$c$$$ is a subarray of an array $$$b$$$ if $$$c$$$ can be obtained from $$$b$$$ by deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) elements from the beginning and several (possibly, zero or all) elements from the end."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call a nonempty array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if for every nonempty subarray of this array, sum of the elements of this subarray is nonzero. For example, array $$$[-1, 2, -3]$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", as all arrays $$$[-1]$$$, $$$[-1, 2]$$$, $$$[-1, 2, -3]$$$, $$$[2]$$$, $$$[2, -3]$$$, $$$[-3]$$$ have nonzero sums of elements. However, array $$$[-1, 2, -1, -3]$$$ isn't "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", as his subarray $$$[-1, 2, -1]$$$ has sum of elements equal to $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help Eugene to calculate the number of nonempty "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" subarrays of a given array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\times 10^5$$$)  — the length of array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of the input contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$)  — the elements of $$$a$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer  — the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" subarrays of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 2 -3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n41 -41 41\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, the following subarrays are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":": $$$[1]$$$, $$$[1, 2]$$$, $$$[2]$$$, $$$[2, -3]$$$, $$$[-3]$$$. However, the subarray $$$[1, 2, -3]$$$ isn't "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", as its subarray $$$[1, 2, -3]$$$ has sum of elements equal to $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample, three subarrays of size 1 are the only "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" subarrays. At the same time, the subarray $$$[41, -41, 41]$$$ isn't "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", as its subarray $$$[41, -41]$$$ has sum of elements equal to $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1333C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1333/problem/C"}